  "report": "The supplied updated set contains explicit Experiment acquisition in three focal accounts: A04, A05 and A11, totaling six product acquisition/checkout/stock-up assertions (four + one + one). These are categories narrated per account, not purchase-event or unit counts. A01 reports cart readdition only; A14 reports gifted receipt; A12 concerns Regimen Lab. The initial-stage roster and separate initial-stage record are not supplied, so an exact historical stage comparison cannot be established without inventing that boundary.\n\nA04 narrates ordering Super Saturated after a sister’s introduction and favorable experience, buying Buffer Jelly for greater nighttime hydration/repair, then buying face wash and mesh moisturizer. The latter products are contextually identifiable as Plasma Wash and Molecular Mesh; exact purchased variants/formulas are unknown. Lightweight hydration before makeup, favorable overnight skin appearance, cleansing and hydration outcomes accompany this expansion. Counter colors also delight the reviewer, but are not explicitly isolated as a purchase trigger. The Super Saturated refill metadata does not establish another acquisition or a narrated repurchase. A05 explicitly checked out Avant Guard after TikTok discovery, within a sustainability-driven account of having stopped disposable sheet masks. A11 explicitly stocked up on Softwear while loving it; three unopened tubes and a reported $70 CAD loss remain after an adverse reaction.\n\nThese three credited Junip customer origins independently repeat the broad proposition of completed Experiment acquisition, across three source accounts in one source role. They do not independently repeat one precise product-specific buying reason. A04 and A11 support the broader reported pattern of favorable experience accompanying subsequent buying, with different products and outcomes. Sustainability/TikTok discovery is one actor’s account; sister introduction is another’s. A01 explicitly attributes returning Softwear to a cart to a comment, but gives no checkout evidence. No focal evidence establishes a general causal effect, representative buying prevalence or cross-venue corroboration of completed Experiment buying.\n\nMaterial context, outside focal counts: cowrunamuck (Reddit t1_nclxocd, 2025-09-05, score 21) reports two Softwear backups because of affection for it and earlier ordering difficulty; praises smoothness, moisture and scent-free performance versus Eadem, and welcomes Sephora availability. This independently adds contextual support for Softwear stocking alongside A11, while preserving opposite tolerability experiences. RowanVC (t1_ncls0z6, same thread/date, score 42) praises Softwear and Experiment, but describes Dr. Idriss exfoliator as sticky and requiring a layer, often lanolin or another mask. This resolves A02’s aversion to the Dr. Idriss exfoliator; it is not Experiment rejection. A02’s short reply reports its own skipping behavior and liking baste balm, not detailed corroboration of Softwear performance. Neither parent donates purchase or use testimony to its focal reply. The Regimen Lab thread resolves A12’s cream 2.0 and cleanser acquisitions as other-brand actions; its post author, date and engagement are unavailable in the supplied context.\n\nAdverse outcomes coexist with loyalty. A11 reports months of satisfaction, morning dead-skin removal, liking the thick texture and sheen, then dermatitis requiring prescribed steroid cream and a worse flare within 24 hours of retrying Softwear. The reviewer attributes causation to Softwear; this is individual self-attribution, not independently confirmed medical causation. Affection and qualified encouragement to try it persist alongside the stock-up loss. A15 contemplated returning Plasma Wash after severe eye burning, poor cleansing and dryness across multiple application methods; no completed return is reported. This conflicts with A04’s favorable face-wash account, yielding mixed reported performance with versions and explanatory conditions unresolved. A14’s gifted Buffer Jelly praise follows only two uses mixed into moisturizer at night with rosacea; it does not isolate Buffer Jelly’s effect or establish paid conversion. A16 intends Continuum to replace azelaic- and salicylic-acid products for simplicity; actual replacement and buying are unreported. A04’s ‘no more makeup remover needed’ establishes reported functional redundancy, not completed routine substitution. A05 explicitly reports already discontinuing sheet masks; that is the completed routine-discontinuation count, not proof that Avant Guard caused the earlier cessation.\n\nObserved engagement: A01/A02/A12 have Reddit scores 13/4/12, marked not interpreted and not materially positive; the contextual parents have scores 21/42 without sufficient exposure context to assign material resonance. Each of the six focal Junip reviews has 0 up-votes and 0 down-votes. Engagement observation times are unavailable. These metrics do not verify experiences, independent origins or buying effects. Distinct Reddit handles are visible, but focal independence is marked unavailable; the shared thread remains shared context. Review update timestamps do not establish additional testimony or events. Formula versions generally remain unknown; verified-buyer metadata alone is excluded from acquisition counts.",
