      "key": "A01",
      "findings": "boxybrown84; Reddit 1n9da6u:ncm3hhd, 2025-09-05; score 13, observation time unavailable, independence unavailable. Removed Experiment balm from FF cart, then explicitly readded it because of a comment. Parent context identifies Softwear and supplies cowrunamuck’s own two-backup account (score 21), not A01’s acquisition or experience. One cart action; no checkout, purchase or use established; variant/formula unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "A02",
      "findings": "PamelaDamnela; Reddit 1n9da6u:ncly8vq, 2025-09-05; score 4, observation time unavailable, independence unavailable. Owns but always skips ‘that one’ because of its feel and likes baste balm. RowanVC parent (score 42) resolves the disliked item to Dr. Idriss exfoliator, describing stickiness and layering; parent separately praises Softwear. No Experiment acquisition or rejection; habitual skipping does not explicitly narrate a completed substitution or prior-routine discontinuation."
    },
    {
      "key": "A04",
      "findings": "Junip customer 202931541, review 7540631, 2025-03-22, updated 2025-03-23; credited origin; votes 0 up/0 down, observation time unavailable. Four narrated acquisitions: Super Saturated after sister introduction/favorable experience; Buffer Jelly for nighttime hydration/repair; face wash, contextually Plasma Wash; mesh moisturizer, contextually Molecular Mesh. Praises pre-makeup hydration, overnight glow, small amounts needed, makeup removal, hydration, no further breakouts and colorful packaging. Reasons are not independently isolated causal effects. ‘No more makeup remover needed’ is functional redundancy, not explicit completed replacement. Review target Super Saturated Refill and Combo + Sensitive metadata add scope, not another purchase. Purchased variants/formulas unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "A05",
      "findings": "Junip customer 44968672, review 1569510, 2022-11-03; credited origin; votes 0/0, observation time unavailable. Explicit Avant Guard checkout after TikTok creator discovery in a sustainability context; one acquisition assertion. Had already stopped formerly near-nightly sheet masks: explicit routine discontinuation, not proven caused by Avant Guard. Almost fits except cheeks/nose; easy cleaning; motivates joint use of hydrating/moisturizing products credited with barrier repair. Metadata identifies Acid Lime/SMALL and verified buyer; it supplies no additional action. Formula/version unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "A12",
      "findings": "eratch; Reddit 1i30kik:m7j6no0, 2025-01-16; score 12, observation time unavailable, independence unavailable. Context identifies Regimen Lab: obtained cream 2.0 seeking healing after excessive tret use and also picked up cleanser. Favorable experience/formulation impressions motivate intent to try more, especially serums/moisturizers; cleanser nice but small. Other-brand acquisition and prospective exploration, not Experiment buying. Context-post identity/time/engagement unavailable."
    },
    {
      "key": "A11",
      "findings": "Junip customer 178058824, review 6638709, 2024-11-25; credited origin; votes 0/0, observation time unavailable. One explicit Softwear stock-up category while delighted, leaving three unopened tubes and reported $70 CAD loss; units are not event counts. Influencer recommendation preceded use, without explicit influencer-caused purchase. Loved thick feel/sheen despite daily dead-skin removal, then reports dermatitis after months, prescribed steroid cream, recovery and worse flare within 24 hours of retry. Product causation is reviewer-attributed. Continued affection and qualified recommendation coexist with harm; no completed return or explicit routine substitution. Formula unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "A14",
      "findings": "Junip customer 344086099, review 8950945, 2025-08-05, updated 2025-08-20; credited origin; votes 0/0, observation time unavailable. Explicit free Buffer Jelly receipt for an honest review; no paid acquisition. After two uses, praises jelly-to-oil slip and softness/no redness, irritation or clogged pores with a drop mixed into nighttime moisturizer and rosacea. Joint use limits attribution. Post-dermaplaning benefit and bottle longevity are expectations; initial bottle-size surprise accompanies claimed full 1 oz. ‘Experiment convert’ is enthusiasm, not buying. Metadata says rewarded=false/verified_buyer=false; it does not negate disclosed gifting. Version unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "A15",
      "findings": "Junip customer 210150638, review 6567933, 2024-11-04; credited origin; votes 0/0, observation time unavailable. Plasma Wash texture praised, but repeated wet/dry, quantity and lathering variations reportedly failed to cleanse/foam and caused severe eye burning; one wash felt less clean/moisturized than unnamed glycerin cleanser, two drier. Considered return; no completed return or narrated acquisition. Questions defect or technique amid social-media praise. Opposes A04’s favorable cleansing account; versions and explanation unresolved. Verified-buyer metadata alone does not count as buying."
    },
    {
      "key": "A16",
      "findings": "Junip customer 529373073, review 13599983, 2026-05-29, updated 2026-06-11; credited origin; votes 0/0, observation time unavailable. Continuum use: easy packaging, mild chemical smell, light gel-serum, no sensitivity, enthusiasm for parabens/science-first formulation, somewhat less-red active acne next morning. Explicitly cannot assess acne/pigmentation efficacy objectively. Prospective replacement of existing azelaic/salicylic-acid products for simplicity and intended staple status; no completed substitution or acquisition. ‘First Time’/verified-buyer metadata does not supply buying testimony; version unknown."
    }
